# Line endings are load-bearing in this repo, so they are pinned rather than left
# to each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Two things hash raw file bytes:
#   1. design-sync's verification anchor. `sourceKeyFor` in its lib/sync-hashes.mjs
#      hashes .design-sync/previews/*.tsx byte-for-byte, and the generated
#      <Name>.prompt.md inherits whatever line endings the preview had. A CRLF
#      checkout therefore invalidates a component's verified state and forces a
#      re-grade with no semantic change — on a fresh Windows clone, all 37 at
#      once. Diagnosed Jul 2026; see .design-sync/NOTES.md.
#   2. dist/ is generated AND committed (the Jinja apps have no Node toolchain).
#      The build writes LF; without this file every regeneration shows the whole
#      tree as modified with an empty content diff.
#
# eol=lf, not text=auto: the working copy must be LF on every platform, because
# that is what the hashes were recorded from.

*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf

# Fonts and images must never be touched.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
